  "summary": "Shift status is widened from max to nvarchar(450) and gets a filtered unique index on Status=\"Open\", enforcing at most one open shift. Customer and CustomerAddress tables are created; Customer.Phone is unique; address rows cascade on customer deletion, and address/phone indices are declared. The delivery address/service values added to Orders are optional snapshots, with ServiceId/Name remaining scalar text rather than an FK. No backfill is needed for nullable snapshot fields. No issue found from this source alone; uniqueness depends on phone canonicalization at write boundary, which this migration cannot establish.",
